    "explanation": "To both parties: this case goes to a human reviewer, and the 37.55 SGD in dispute is held — not collected from the rider and not refunded to her — until that review. Here is why.\n\nWhat is settled. The trip did leave the recommended route. On the platform's recorded distances (POL-RD-22): 22.9 km actual minus 21.3 km recommended = 1.60 km of deviation. That is over the 1.0 km tolerance but under the 2.0 km ceiling in POL-RD-25, so the distance alone does not send this to a human. The LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-05011-01 (weight 1.0) is a real ACCIDENT on the PIE towards Changi after the Adam Road exit, live 07:44–08:54 and so overlapping the trip; that is the PIE leg of the recommended route, in the direction of travel, at the very point where the driver left it — so the reroute is traffic-justified under POL-RD-23. The GPS trace EV-GPS-05011 (weight 1.0) shows which route was taken and when, and per POL-RD-22 is not used to re-measure the distance, so it cannot shrink the 1.60 km.\n\nWhat cannot be settled, and decides the case. POL-RD-24 turns on whether the driver informed the rider before or at the point of deviation (POL-RD-21). Row (a) — no refund — needs the rider informed and agreeing; row (b) — refund of the excess distance fare — needs her not informed. That fact rests on one artifact, the in-app chat EV-CHAT-05011, which the pre-pass marks IMPAIRED, weight 0.4, issue CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT: the driver's reroute message MSG-05011-003 carries a driver-device sent_at of 08:10:49 (before the 08:12:19 deviation) and a server delivered_at of 08:14:19 (after it), and the entry's own read receipt of 08:11:13 cannot precede its delivery. The two clocks straddle the deviation and nothing in the record says which is right, so it cannot be established whether the notice came before the turn or after it. The rider's 'ok can' reply sits in the same impaired log. The driver's own account in the dispute is a bare assertion, and POL-RD-21 says a notice not backed by the chat log or a call recording cannot be established. An undecided limb supports neither the no-refund row nor the refund row, so no row of POL-RD-24 fits; POL-RD-24 and POL-GEN-26 both send such a case to a human reviewer.\n\nMoney. The most any row of the matrix could return is the excess distance fare, 1.60 km × 0.72 SGD/km = 1.15 SGD (rows (b)/(d)); row (a) would return nothing; and no row returns the whole 37.55 SGD fare the rider asks for (metered total 37.55 = base 2.80 + distance 16.49 + time 6.21 + ERP 3.50 + platform fee 0.90, plus surge 7.65). None of those amounts is ordered today.\n\nConfidence. The pivotal fact is carried only by the 0.4 chat log, so confidence is capped at 0.40 (POL-GEN-02(2)), below the 0.80 that POL-GEN-22 and POL-RD-25 require on a 37.55 SGD route deviation. Neither profile carries a fraud flag, so 0.80 and not 0.95 is the bar. No route-deviation clause in this version produces a referral.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: which of MSG-05011-003's timestamps is correct — did the driver's reroute message reach the rider before 08:12:19, or only after the vehicle had already left the recommended route?"
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "If the judge finds the notice fact genuinely unestablished rather than established as late, then the open question is one POL-GEN-26 names in terms - whether the driver notified the rider - and the only artifact that would answer it is impaired at 0.4, so under POL-GEN-02(2) confidence on the deciding fact cannot pass 0.4 and falls below the 0.80 that POL-GEN-22 requires on a 37.55 SGD dispute. The same is true of whether the accident advisory intersects the recommended route, which the package itself leaves undetermined for the judge. On that reading the case escalates and the 37.55 SGD is held rather than collected, which leaves the rider not carrying the disputed charge while a human reviews it; the rider's alternative to the 1.15 SGD refund above is escalation, not NO_ACTION.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-CHAT-05011 at weight_multiplier 0.4 but does not name its issue code(s): CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT"
    },
